    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# KINROOT · Website ↔ n8n Social Sourcing\n\n**Workflow is dynamic**, not hardcoded to one clip. Run it by uploading the PDF in the Kinroot website and clicking **Start n8n social search**.\n\n1. Import this JSON into the *same local n8n* running alongside your Kinroot Docker website.\n2. Reconnect **Bearer Auth** in all 3 Apify HTTP nodes and **Query Auth** in the YouTube HTTP node. Credentials are intentionally absent from this file.\n3. **Publish** workflow to activate production webhook `/webhook/kinroot-source`.\n4. Restart the updated website: `docker compose -f compose.clip-review.yaml up -d --build`.\n5. Run **one clip** first; every new clip can start 3 Apify Actors and 1 YouTube API request. Actor runs may incur charges or exhaust free credits.\n\nCandidate results go to the website, where Groq can rank their metadata. This does NOT mean legal rights, HD quality, or visual scene match have been proven.\n\n**Facebook** requires a separate verified keyword-search provider. Facebook page-based scrapers are not generic search. No fake Facebook actor is included.\n\nDownloading third-party videos is NOT silently enabled. Supported direct media can be acquired and trimmed only after rights confirmation. No bypassing access restrictions.\n",
        "height": 485,
        "width": 690,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "bd5c4def-320e-480f-934e-57068a6f1bb0",
      "name": "START HERE — IMPORTANT",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -900,
        -670
      ]
    }
